/-!
# Terminal H14--D11 canonical-Schwarz nuclear-Duhamel zeta facade

This is the strongest independent terminal facade currently implemented in PR
#60.  It imports the complete preferred Candidate-A route from the concrete H14
reduced Green operator through the D11 unitary frame to the physical
five-sector spectral-cut atlas.

The actual heat/zeta family is generated by unitary transport.  Every reference
family is generated from intrinsic nuclear operator spectra, rank-one Duhamel
simplex averages, cyclic semigroup collapse, short/long coefficient integrals,
a differentiable rank-one counterterm, and endpoint limits.

Schwarz symmetry in the Mellin convergence half-plane is now canonical:

* pointwise kernel conjugation is algebraic for a real heat trace;
* integrability is already part of the Mellin continuation packet;
* complex conjugation is bundled as a real continuous linear map and moved
  through the Bochner integral;
* Gamma conjugation is supplied by Mathlib.

Thus the only remaining complex reflection datum per reference is a common
open preconnected domain containing zero and a Mellin seed, together with
analyticity of the continuation and of

```text
s ↦ conj (zeta (conj s)).
```

The chain derives all of the following:

```text
Tr(D_a(t)) = integral_s Tr(D_a(t,s)) dμ(s),
Tr(D_a(t,s)) = Tr(H'_a K_a(t)),
integral_t Tr(D_a(t)) = Tr(D_region,a),
counterterm derivative = Tr(C'_a),
C'_a - D_short,a = G_a H'_a + B_a,
D_long,a = B_a,
FP'_a = Tr(G_a H'_a),
I_a(s) = conj (I_a(conj s)),
M_a(s) = conj (M_a(conj s)),
Im (zeta'_a(0)) = 0,
T_reference,a = -Tr(G_a H'_a),
T_relative,a = Tr(G_ref,a H'_ref,a).
```

The remaining irreducible reference-side work is now concentrated in:

1. concrete construction and intrinsic nuclear estimates for the reference
   heat and Duhamel operators;
2. summability and the three spectral sum/integral exchanges;
3. the heat semigroup law and slice identifications;
4. short-time renormalized convergence and long-time primitive decay;
5. analytic regularity of the reflected continuation on the selected common
   domain.

No scalar trace comparison, Mellin-conjugation equality, endpoint identity,
finite-part derivative, zeta reality or connection-coefficient equality remains
as an input of this terminal interface.
-/

